<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The AdMob application id.

  Not optional once the ads SDK is on the classpath: it is read out of the
  manifest when the app starts, and a build without it crashes on launch
  rather than merely failing to show an ad.

  This is the real app id. Unlike the unit ids in lib/data/ads.dart it is the
  same in debug and release, and it has to be: the SDK validates it at start
  up, and a test app id paired with the real units a release build uses would
  simply serve nothing.

  That is safe because an app id on its own shows no ads and earns nothing —
  only a unit id does, and every unit is switched to Google's test inventory
  by kDebugMode. What must never happen is a debug build pointing at a real
  unit: Google counts a developer's own impressions as invalid traffic, and
  that is the usual way an AdMob account gets suspended.

  If the game ships on iOS it needs its own AdMob app, and
  GADApplicationIdentifier in ios/Runner/Info.plist has to hold that one
  rather than a copy of this.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="admob_app_id" translatable="false">ca-app-pub-8244651657160773~5919462505</string>
</resources>
